# Project Overview

- This repository is a new Symfony CMS Engine for `zaborprofil.ru`, replacing WordPress.
- Do not build WordPress importers, shortcode parsers, Laravel code, Docker setup, or EasyAdmin as the primary admin UI.
- The app lives at repository root. The web root is `public_html/`, not Symfony's default `public/`.
- Public pages must be server-rendered with Symfony + Twig for SEO; do not turn the public site into a pure SPA.
- The target stack is PHP `>=8.5`, Node.js `>=25.9.0` (npm `>=11.12.1`), nginx `>=1.30.0`, Symfony `8.x`, PostgreSQL `>=18`, Redis `>=8`, Doctrine, Twig, Tailwind CSS, Vite, React admin SPA (`admin/`).
- Documentation must be written in Russian.
- Development database state must be reproducible from Doctrine migrations plus fixtures/seed data. Do not commit Docker images, Docker volumes, real PostgreSQL backups, production/staging dumps, uploads, secrets, or personal data. Only a small manually reviewed anonymized dev snapshot is allowed in Git when fixtures are not enough.

## Main Directories

- `src/Shared/` contains shared contracts, value objects, infrastructure adapters, and shared UI entrypoints.
- `src/Module/` contains bounded modules of the modular monolith.
- `templates/` contains Twig templates.
- `assets/site/` contains public site assets.
- `admin/` contains React admin SPA assets (Vite entry `admin/app.ts`).
- `docs/` contains Russian project documentation.

